REQ-6-3-1 Implementation Report
================================

Requirement: View Pull Request Overview and Commits

Status: COMPLETE

The requirement is fully implemented in the existing workspace. No code
changes were required; the previous node failure was due to the agent
exceeding the 40-iteration limit, not an acceptance failure.

Implementation details:

1. PR detail page (frontend/src/pull-request.html)
   - Unified read view for a given PR number, reached via
     /pull-request?org=&repo=&number=
   - Displays the PR title in an <h1> heading (exact title).
   - Meta line shows "#number · state · author wants to merge headBranch
     into baseBranch" (base/compare branches).
   - Three tabs: "Conversation", "Commits", "Files changed" — all rendered
     as <a> links (role=tablist), so they are navigable links.
   - Tab state is preserved in the URL query (?tab=...) and via
     history.replaceState, so reloading preserves the active tab and the
     heading.
   - Conversation tab: shows description (pr-body), activity/status events,
     discussion comments, checks ("test: status"), and reviews.
   - Commits tab: shows "Commit summary" heading and the list of comparable
     commits (head branch commits not present in base branch).
   - Files changed tab: shows "Changed files summary" heading and the list
     of changed files with +additions/-deletions, each linking to /diff.
   - Viewing operations are read-only; they do not create comments, reviews,
     or merges.

2. PR list page (frontend/src/pull-requests.html)
   - PR titles link to the detail page (/pull-request?org=&repo=&number=).

3. Backend (backend/server.js)
   - GET /api/repo/pull-request?org=&repo=&number= returns the PR detail
     including title, body, state, author, base/head branches, activity,
     comments, reviews, check, comparable commits, and changed files.
   - Public repositories are readable without sign-in (canReadRepo /
     canAccessRepo return true for non-private repos).
   - Comparable commits are computed as head-branch commits not present in
     the base branch (by commit id).
   - Changed files are computed by diffing base vs head branch file contents.

4. Seed data
   - PR #1 "Improve onboarding" (open) in acme-docs (public org repo):
     - title: "Improve onboarding"
     - description: "Improve the onboarding flow for new users."
     - discussion comment from bob-reviewer
     - at least one comparable commit ("Add search feature" on
       feature-search branch relative to main)
     - check "test" with status pending
   - PR #2 "Fix search" (closed)
   - PR #3 "Draft onboarding update" (draft)
   - Branches: main, feature-search, draft-feature
   - Reviewer: bob-reviewer

All three scenarios of REQ-6-3-1 are satisfied:
- Scenario 1: unauthenticated reviewer opens the Open PR and switches among
  Conversation, Commits, and Files changed tabs; all refer to the same PR
  number; refresh preserves title, branches, commits; no writes occur.
- Scenario 2/3: signed-in user (alice-dev) follows the same workflow; the
  page displays required headings/controls/values; refresh/reopen preserves
  the persisted result.

No changes were needed. The dist build (frontend/dist) is in sync with src.
